WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.215 --> 00:00:03.388
Diane Okafor: Okay, I've started the recording.

2
00:00:03.643 --> 00:00:06.154
Diane Okafor: Can everybody hear me all right?

3
00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:09.537
Raymond Castillo: Yep, you're good, Diane.

4
00:00:10.347 --> 00:00:11.561
Marcus Bell: Loud and clear.

5
00:00:12.911 --> 00:00:13.461
Diane Okafor: Great.

6
00:00:13.692 --> 00:00:18.856
Diane Okafor: Grace, I can see you, but I think you're still on mute.

7
00:00:23.446 --> 00:00:24.348
Grace Lindqvist: Sorry, sorry.

8
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:26.696
Grace Lindqvist: Can you hear me now?

9
00:00:27.641 --> 00:00:29.348
Diane Okafor: Yes, we've got you.

10
00:00:29.589 --> 00:00:31.802
Diane Okafor: Priya, are you with us?

11
00:00:33.287 --> 00:00:34.148
Priya Raman: I'm here.

12
00:00:34.343 --> 00:00:40.215
Priya Raman: Just so everyone knows, I sent out an updated financial package about an hour ago.

13
00:00:40.319 --> 00:00:47.281
Priya Raman: So if you're looking at the packet from last week, the reserve page changed a little bit.

14
00:00:48.361 --> 00:00:49.662
Diane Okafor: Okay, thanks, Priya.

15
00:00:49.981 --> 00:00:52.655
Diane Okafor: I haven't heard from Helen yet.

16
00:00:52.714 --> 00:00:57.439
Diane Okafor: She texted that she might be a few minutes late,

17
00:00:57.504 --> 00:01:03.693
Diane Okafor: so let's give it another minute or so and then we'll get going.

18
00:01:16.518 --> 00:01:21.724
Marcus Bell: Um, I think there are a couple more people in the waiting room.

19
00:01:22.939 --> 00:01:25.257
Priya Raman: Yep, I'm letting them in now.

20
00:01:33.357 --> 00:01:37.135
Raymond Castillo: Diane, did you get my email about the gate?

21
00:01:37.361 --> 00:01:39.387
Raymond Castillo: I sent it this afternoon.

22
00:01:40.602 --> 00:01:41.551
Diane Okafor: I did.

23
00:01:41.773 --> 00:01:48.254
Diane Okafor: Priya's going to cover it in her report, so let's hold it until then.

24
00:02:07.154 --> 00:02:07.996
Diane Okafor: All right.

25
00:02:08.051 --> 00:02:12.292
Diane Okafor: It's 7:02, so let's go ahead and get started.

26
00:02:14.317 --> 00:02:15.704
Diane Okafor: Good evening, everyone.

27
00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:24.181
Diane Okafor: I'm going to call this regular meeting of the Renfield Commons Homeowners Association Board of Directors to order.

28
00:02:24.431 --> 00:02:25.702
Diane Okafor: It's 7:02 p.m.

29
00:02:26.005 --> 00:02:32.240
Diane Okafor: Just a reminder that we record these meetings so that Marcus can prepare the minutes,

30
00:02:32.307 --> 00:02:36.829
Diane Okafor: and we delete the recording once the minutes are approved.

31
00:02:36.995 --> 00:02:42.737
Diane Okafor: If you're a homeowner and you'd like to speak during the open forum,

32
00:02:43.011 --> 00:02:49.727
Diane Okafor: please use the raise hand button and Priya will unmute you when it's your turn.

33
00:02:50.807 --> 00:02:53.066
Diane Okafor: Before we start, one announcement.

34
00:02:53.312 --> 00:03:01.169
Diane Okafor: The annual meeting and election is on December 9th, and the call for candidates goes out next week.

35
00:03:01.358 --> 00:03:06.710
Diane Okafor: If you're interested in serving on the board, please watch your email.

36
00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.293
Diane Okafor: Marcus, would you call the roll?

37
00:03:11.373 --> 00:03:11.923
Marcus Bell: Sure.

38
00:03:12.007 --> 00:03:12.860
Marcus Bell: Diane Okafor?

39
00:03:13.535 --> 00:03:14.085
Diane Okafor: Here.

40
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:15.632
Marcus Bell: Raymond Castillo?

41
00:03:16.442 --> 00:03:16.992
Raymond Castillo: Here.

42
00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:18.558
Marcus Bell: Grace Lindquist?

43
00:03:19.503 --> 00:03:20.053
Grace Lindqvist: Present.

44
00:03:20.728 --> 00:03:21.625
Marcus Bell: Helen Whitaker?

45
00:03:25.135 --> 00:03:25.984
Marcus Bell: Not yet.

46
00:03:26.127 --> 00:03:28.155
Marcus Bell: And Marcus Bell is here.

47
00:03:28.324 --> 00:03:31.176
Marcus Bell: So that's four of our five directors.

48
00:03:32.391 --> 00:03:33.293
Diane Okafor: Thank you.

49
00:03:33.557 --> 00:03:38.287
Diane Okafor: We need three for a quorum, so we have a quorum.

50
00:03:38.599 --> 00:03:44.625
Diane Okafor: Also with us tonight is Priya Raman from Hartwell and Finch, our community manager.

51
00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:48.754
Diane Okafor: And I count nine homeowners on the call.

52
00:03:49.022 --> 00:03:51.745
Diane Okafor: Welcome, everybody, and thanks for coming.

53
00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:55.726
Diane Okafor: Next is approval of the agenda.

54
00:03:55.847 --> 00:03:58.842
Diane Okafor: Everyone should have it in the packet.

55
00:03:58.896 --> 00:04:02.793
Diane Okafor: Are there any changes or additions to the agenda?

56
00:04:08.463 --> 00:04:09.013
Diane Okafor: Okay.

57
00:04:09.094 --> 00:04:12.642
Diane Okafor: Hearing none, the agenda is approved as presented.

58
00:04:13.722 --> 00:04:17.196
Diane Okafor: That brings us to the homeowner open forum.

59
00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:20.249
Diane Okafor: We set aside ten minutes for this,

60
00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:25.758
Diane Okafor: and we ask that each speaker keep it to about three minutes.

61
00:04:26.042 --> 00:04:32.784
Diane Okafor: The board will listen, and if something needs action, we'll put it on a future agenda.

62
00:04:32.837 --> 00:04:36.134
Diane Okafor: Priya, do we have any hands up?

63
00:04:37.754 --> 00:04:39.806
Priya Raman: We have three hands up.

64
00:04:39.976 --> 00:04:41.935
Priya Raman: The first is Kevin T.

65
00:04:42.257 --> 00:04:44.185
Priya Raman: Kevin, I'm unmuting you now.

66
00:04:47.965 --> 00:04:48.848
Kevin T: Hi, thanks.

67
00:04:49.028 --> 00:04:51.120
Kevin T: Can you hear me okay?

68
00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:54.019
Diane Okafor: We can hear you fine.

69
00:04:54.964 --> 00:04:55.514
Kevin T: Great.

70
00:04:55.817 --> 00:05:00.984
Kevin T: So, Kevin Tran, I'm on Wrenfield Drive, up near the north entrance.

71
00:05:01.075 --> 00:05:04.546
Kevin T: I want to bring up the speeding again.

72
00:05:04.870 --> 00:05:12.198
Kevin T: People are cutting through to Route 9 in the morning and they are doing forty, forty-five, easy.

73
00:05:12.285 --> 00:05:17.681
Kevin T: School just started and we have a lot of kids on bikes now.

74
00:05:17.852 --> 00:05:24.625
Kevin T: I know we talked about speed bumps last year and that kind of went nowhere,

75
00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:30.571
Kevin T: but what about one of those radar signs that shows you your speed?

76
00:05:30.734 --> 00:05:32.827
Kevin T: Or even just more signs.

77
00:05:33.043 --> 00:05:33.876
Kevin T: Anything, honestly.

78
00:05:35.091 --> 00:05:40.455
Kevin T: Oh, and if you do get signs, they'd probably need to be solar.

79
00:05:40.563 --> 00:05:43.502
Kevin T: There's no power out by the entrance.

80
00:05:44.852 --> 00:05:45.794
Diane Okafor: Thanks, Kevin.

81
00:05:46.039 --> 00:05:50.222
Diane Okafor: I agree it's a real problem, I see it too.

82
00:05:50.409 --> 00:05:55.422
Diane Okafor: The speed bumps were difficult because of the snow plow contract,

83
00:05:55.622 --> 00:05:59.357
Diane Okafor: but the radar signs are a good idea.

84
00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:07.227
Diane Okafor: Priya, could you get us a couple of quotes on radar speed signs before the next meeting?

85
00:06:08.307 --> 00:06:08.857
Priya Raman: Sure.

86
00:06:09.087 --> 00:06:13.815
Priya Raman: And good point on the solar, I'll ask for solar models.

87
00:06:14.074 --> 00:06:19.565
Priya Raman: I'll get quotes for two signs, one at each end of Wrenfield Drive,

88
00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:23.165
Priya Raman: and I'll have them in the October packet.

89
00:06:23.975 --> 00:06:25.274
Kevin T: That'd be great.

90
00:06:25.544 --> 00:06:26.344
Kevin T: Thank you.

91
00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:30.208
Priya Raman: Next we have J Moreno.

92
00:06:30.282 --> 00:06:32.037
Priya Raman: Go ahead, you're unmuted.

93
00:06:35.007 --> 00:06:35.557
J Moreno: Hi.

94
00:06:35.833 --> 00:06:39.660
J Moreno: Um, hi, this is Julia Moreno on Thistle Court.

95
00:06:39.808 --> 00:06:43.002
J Moreno: Mine's about dog waste around the playground.

96
00:06:43.316 --> 00:06:50.139
J Moreno: There's no bag station anywhere near it, and people just aren't picking up after their dogs.

97
00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:54.559
J Moreno: My kids have stepped in it twice this month.

98
00:06:54.787 --> 00:06:58.266
J Moreno: Could we put a station by the playground?

99
00:06:59.481 --> 00:07:01.072
Raymond Castillo: That's a fair point.

100
00:07:01.284 --> 00:07:05.289
Raymond Castillo: The closest one is down by the mailboxes, right?

101
00:07:06.099 --> 00:07:13.398
J Moreno: Right, by the mailboxes, which is kind of far if you're over on that side.

102
00:07:14.613 --> 00:07:15.163
Diane Okafor: Okay.

103
00:07:15.236 --> 00:07:22.829
Diane Okafor: Can somebody look at whether we can add a station by the playground, and what it would cost?

104
00:07:23.774 --> 00:07:26.710
Raymond Castillo: Yeah, I mean, we could probably, uh,

105
00:07:26.110 --> 00:07:27.473
Grace Lindqvist: They're not expensive.

106
00:07:27.538 --> 00:07:30.672
Grace Lindqvist: I think they're a couple hundred dollars.

107
00:07:31.752 --> 00:07:32.302
Diane Okafor: Okay.

108
00:07:32.359 --> 00:07:36.546
Diane Okafor: Let's, let's get that figured out for next month.

109
00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:38.054
Diane Okafor: Thank you, Julia.

110
00:07:38.729 --> 00:07:39.593
J Moreno: Thank you.

111
00:07:41.348 --> 00:07:44.209
Priya Raman: And the last hand is Annette Wu.

112
00:07:47.449 --> 00:07:48.340
Annette Wu: Hi everyone.

113
00:07:48.412 --> 00:07:50.498
Annette Wu: This is a quick one.

114
00:07:50.795 --> 00:07:55.461
Annette Wu: The pool closed on the 8th, right after Labor Day,

115
00:07:55.716 --> 00:08:00.277
Annette Wu: and it was still like eighty-five degrees the whole next week.

116
00:08:00.458 --> 00:08:06.976
Annette Wu: Is there any way we could keep it open through the end of September next year?

117
00:08:07.077 --> 00:08:12.403
Annette Wu: I think a lot of people would use it on the weekends.

118
00:08:13.618 --> 00:08:15.329
Diane Okafor: That's a good question.

119
00:08:15.568 --> 00:08:22.847
Diane Okafor: The lifeguard contract and the chemicals are budgeted through Labor Day, so it's really a budget question.

120
00:08:23.013 --> 00:08:30.524
Diane Okafor: We'll be working on the 2027 budget in October and November, so let's take it up then.

121
00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:35.739
Grace Lindqvist: I'll add it to the list for the budget workshop.

122
00:08:36.549 --> 00:08:37.455
Annette Wu: Okay, great.

123
00:08:37.533 --> 00:08:38.083
Annette Wu: Thanks.

124
00:08:39.433 --> 00:08:40.780
Diane Okafor: Thank you all.

125
00:08:40.997 --> 00:08:43.191
Diane Okafor: That closes the open forum.

126
00:08:44.811 --> 00:08:50.226
Diane Okafor: Item five is approval of the minutes from the August 19th meeting.

127
00:08:50.326 --> 00:08:52.034
Diane Okafor: Does anyone have corrections?

128
00:08:53.789 --> 00:08:55.407
Marcus Bell: Yes, I have one.

129
00:08:55.549 --> 00:09:02.628
Marcus Bell: On page two, under the treasurer's report, it says the reserve transfer for July was $4,500.

130
00:09:02.706 --> 00:09:04.372
Marcus Bell: It should be $5,400.

131
00:09:04.664 --> 00:09:10.072
Marcus Bell: I think I just flipped the numbers when I typed it up.

132
00:09:10.882 --> 00:09:11.704
Grace Lindqvist: That's right.

133
00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:13.202
Grace Lindqvist: It was $5,400.

134
00:09:14.282 --> 00:09:14.832
Diane Okafor: Okay.

135
00:09:15.130 --> 00:09:16.411
Diane Okafor: Any other corrections?

136
00:09:20.596 --> 00:09:26.201
Diane Okafor: Then is there a motion to approve the August 19th minutes as corrected?

137
00:09:27.416 --> 00:09:32.274
Marcus Bell: I'll move that we approve the August 19th minutes as corrected.

138
00:09:32.949 --> 00:09:33.499
Raymond Castillo: Second.

139
00:09:34.174 --> 00:09:36.932
Diane Okafor: Moved by Marcus, seconded by Raymond.

140
00:09:37.121 --> 00:09:37.961
Diane Okafor: Any discussion?

141
00:09:41.066 --> 00:09:42.478
Diane Okafor: All in favor?

142
00:09:43.018 --> 00:09:43.568
Raymond Castillo: Aye.

143
00:09:43.368 --> 00:09:43.918
Grace Lindqvist: Aye.

144
00:09:43.818 --> 00:09:44.368
Marcus Bell: Aye.

145
00:09:44.773 --> 00:09:45.323
Diane Okafor: Aye.

146
00:09:45.429 --> 00:09:46.286
Diane Okafor: Any opposed?

147
00:09:46.582 --> 00:09:47.447
Diane Okafor: Any abstentions?

148
00:09:50.417 --> 00:09:50.967
Diane Okafor: Okay.

149
00:09:51.147 --> 00:09:55.162
Diane Okafor: The minutes are approved as corrected, four to nothing.

150
00:09:56.377 --> 00:09:58.152
Diane Okafor: Grace, the treasurer's report.

151
00:09:59.502 --> 00:10:00.327
Grace Lindqvist: Thanks, Diane.

152
00:10:00.465 --> 00:10:05.138
Grace Lindqvist: Priya, could you put the balance sheet up on the screen?

153
00:10:06.083 --> 00:10:07.337
Priya Raman: Sure, one second.

154
00:10:19.487 --> 00:10:21.506
Priya Raman: Okay, can everyone see it?

155
00:10:22.586 --> 00:10:24.909
Diane Okafor: Yes, we can see it.

156
00:10:26.259 --> 00:10:26.809
Grace Lindqvist: Great.

157
00:10:26.864 --> 00:10:30.865
Grace Lindqvist: So these are the August financials, through August 31st.

158
00:10:31.015 --> 00:10:35.616
Grace Lindqvist: Operating cash is $48,212.67, and the reserve accounts total $312,540.18.

159
00:10:35.917 --> 00:10:40.502
Grace Lindqvist: Year to date we're about $3,900 under budget on operating expenses,

160
00:10:40.708 --> 00:10:43.350
Grace Lindqvist: and most of that is water,

161
00:10:43.686 --> 00:10:49.183
Grace Lindqvist: because we had all that rain in July and the irrigation barely ran.

162
00:10:49.993 --> 00:10:55.151
Grace Lindqvist: The one surprise was the pool pump motor, which failed in August.

163
00:10:55.465 --> 00:10:59.894
Grace Lindqvist: That was $1,240, and it came out of pool repairs,

164
00:11:00.121 --> 00:11:04.384
Grace Lindqvist: so that line is now over budget for the year.

165
00:11:04.612 --> 00:11:06.426
Grace Lindqvist: But we're fine overall.

166
00:11:07.371 --> 00:11:13.463
Grace Lindqvist: On delinquencies, we have six accounts more than sixty days past due, totaling $7,850.

167
00:11:13.736 --> 00:11:20.274
Grace Lindqvist: That's down from eight accounts last month, and two of the six are on payment plans.

168
00:11:20.537 --> 00:11:26.299
Grace Lindqvist: And the July reserve transfer of $5,400 did go through, like Marcus said.

169
00:11:27.379 --> 00:11:34.660
Grace Lindqvist: Collections for the month were about 97 percent of the assessments billed, which is normal for us.

170
00:11:34.968 --> 00:11:40.232
Grace Lindqvist: And one heads-up for the budget: the insurance renewal is in December,

171
00:11:40.318 --> 00:11:46.106
Grace Lindqvist: and the broker expects roughly a 12 percent increase on the property policy.

172
00:11:47.321 --> 00:11:48.224
Diane Okafor: Thanks, Grace.

173
00:11:48.453 --> 00:11:49.850
Diane Okafor: Questions for Grace?

174
00:11:52.010 --> 00:11:52.890
Raymond Castillo: Just one.

175
00:11:53.151 --> 00:11:57.788
Raymond Castillo: The pump motor, was that covered by the warranty at all?

176
00:11:58.733 --> 00:12:02.488
Grace Lindqvist: No, it was about six months past the warranty.

177
00:12:02.747 --> 00:12:03.674
Grace Lindqvist: Priya checked.

178
00:12:04.349 --> 00:12:06.659
Priya Raman: Yeah, I called the pool company.

179
00:12:06.804 --> 00:12:07.974
Priya Raman: No luck, unfortunately.

180
00:12:09.459 --> 00:12:14.784
Marcus Bell: And on the delinquencies, are any of those headed to the attorney?

181
00:12:15.864 --> 00:12:21.704
Grace Lindqvist: One of them might be, but let's talk about that in executive session.

182
00:12:23.054 --> 00:12:29.523
Diane Okafor: And on the insurance, is the broker going to shop it around this year?

183
00:12:30.468 --> 00:12:31.018
Grace Lindqvist: Yes.

184
00:12:31.185 --> 00:12:34.399
Grace Lindqvist: She's getting at least two other quotes,

185
00:12:34.474 --> 00:12:39.518
Grace Lindqvist: and she said she'll have numbers for us before the budget workshop.

186
00:12:40.868 --> 00:12:41.418
Diane Okafor: Okay.

187
00:12:41.753 --> 00:12:45.638
Diane Okafor: Is there a motion to accept the treasurer's report?

188
00:12:46.718 --> 00:12:50.397
Marcus Bell: I move we accept the treasurer's report as presented.

189
00:12:51.072 --> 00:12:51.622
Raymond Castillo: Second.

190
00:12:51.122 --> 00:12:51.672
Grace Lindqvist: Second.

191
00:12:52.482 --> 00:12:56.159
Diane Okafor: Okay, we have a motion and a second.

192
00:12:56.417 --> 00:12:57.336
Diane Okafor: Any discussion?

193
00:13:00.036 --> 00:13:01.425
Diane Okafor: All in favor?

194
00:13:01.965 --> 00:13:02.515
Raymond Castillo: Aye.

195
00:13:02.315 --> 00:13:02.865
Marcus Bell: Aye.

196
00:13:02.765 --> 00:13:03.315
Grace Lindqvist: Aye.

197
00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:04.270
Diane Okafor: Aye.

198
00:13:04.335 --> 00:13:04.885
Diane Okafor: Opposed?

199
00:13:07.585 --> 00:13:09.759
Diane Okafor: Hearing none, that carries unanimously.

200
00:13:10.974 --> 00:13:12.777
Diane Okafor: Priya, the manager's report.

201
00:13:13.857 --> 00:13:14.407
Priya Raman: Sure.

202
00:13:14.501 --> 00:13:16.047
Priya Raman: So, a few things.

203
00:13:16.321 --> 00:13:21.991
Priya Raman: The pool closed for the season on September 8th, and the winterizing is done.

204
00:13:22.068 --> 00:13:27.995
Priya Raman: We had 14 work orders since the last meeting, and 11 of them are closed.

205
00:13:28.243 --> 00:13:33.320
Priya Raman: The three open ones are the gate arm at the north entrance,

206
00:13:33.504 --> 00:13:38.544
Priya Raman: which is waiting on a part, an irrigation leak on Thistle Court,

207
00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:44.484
Priya Raman: which the landscaper is fixing this week, and a streetlight that's out on Wrenfield Drive,

208
00:13:44.621 --> 00:13:47.676
Priya Raman: which I reported to the electric company.

209
00:13:49.161 --> 00:13:50.445
Helen's iPhone: Hi, sorry, everyone.

210
00:13:50.574 --> 00:13:51.460
Helen's iPhone: It's Helen.

211
00:13:51.526 --> 00:13:52.863
Helen's iPhone: I'm finally here.

212
00:13:53.110 --> 00:13:59.070
Helen's iPhone: I'm on my phone, so I might be a little hard to hear.

213
00:14:00.015 --> 00:14:00.896
Diane Okafor: Welcome, Helen.

214
00:14:01.105 --> 00:14:04.825
Diane Okafor: Let the minutes show Helen joined at 7:14.

215
00:14:05.500 --> 00:14:06.356
Marcus Bell: Got it.

216
00:14:07.571 --> 00:14:08.400
Priya Raman: Okay, continuing.

217
00:14:08.667 --> 00:14:09.217
Priya Raman: Violations.

218
00:14:09.305 --> 00:14:12.902
Priya Raman: We sent nine courtesy notices in the last month.

219
00:14:13.084 --> 00:14:18.890
Priya Raman: Seven were for trash cans visible from the street, and two were for overgrown lawns.

220
00:14:19.003 --> 00:14:21.303
Priya Raman: Two of those are already resolved.

221
00:14:21.386 --> 00:14:25.881
Priya Raman: And the fall walk-through inspection is scheduled for Saturday, October 3rd.

222
00:14:26.224 --> 00:14:28.178
Priya Raman: Directors are welcome to join.

223
00:14:28.268 --> 00:14:31.344
Priya Raman: We'll start at 9 a.m. at the clubhouse.

224
00:14:32.289 --> 00:14:33.483
Priya Raman: Two smaller things.

225
00:14:33.566 --> 00:14:36.693
Priya Raman: The clubhouse air conditioning was serviced last week,

226
00:14:36.982 --> 00:14:42.074
Priya Raman: and the new locks on the mailbox kiosk on Larkspur Lane are installed.

227
00:14:42.392 --> 00:14:48.569
Priya Raman: Residents who haven't picked up their new keys can get them from the management office.

228
00:14:49.649 --> 00:14:50.517
Diane Okafor: Thanks, Priya.

229
00:14:50.842 --> 00:14:53.557
Diane Okafor: Any questions on the manager's report?

230
00:14:55.447 --> 00:14:56.723
Grace Lindqvist: The gate arm.

231
00:14:56.927 --> 00:15:01.182
Grace Lindqvist: Is it just stuck open until the part comes in?

232
00:15:01.992 --> 00:15:04.490
Priya Raman: It's stuck open right now, yes.

233
00:15:04.739 --> 00:15:10.255
Priya Raman: The vendor said the part should be in by the end of next week.

234
00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:15.797
Raymond Castillo: And the streetlight, did the electric company give you a date?

235
00:15:16.607 --> 00:15:19.603
Priya Raman: They said seven to ten business days.

236
00:15:19.765 --> 00:15:21.395
Priya Raman: I'll keep after them.

237
00:15:22.745 --> 00:15:26.793
Raymond Castillo: And on the gate, that's what my email was about.

238
00:15:26.847 --> 00:15:30.385
Raymond Castillo: It's been stuck open for almost two weeks,

239
00:15:30.678 --> 00:15:35.287
Raymond Castillo: and we've had people dumping yard waste by the dumpsters again.

240
00:15:35.624 --> 00:15:39.461
Raymond Castillo: Is there anything we can do in the meantime?

241
00:15:40.541 --> 00:15:45.722
Priya Raman: I asked the vendor about locking it closed with the keypad working,

242
00:15:46.035 --> 00:15:49.620
Priya Raman: but the arm motor is the part that failed,

243
00:15:49.846 --> 00:15:53.661
Priya Raman: so it really has to wait for the part.

244
00:15:53.941 --> 00:15:58.152
Priya Raman: It should be in by the end of next week.

245
00:15:59.367 --> 00:15:59.917
Diane Okafor: Okay.

246
00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:05.706
Diane Okafor: Let's give it until then, and Priya, just keep us posted by email.

247
00:16:06.381 --> 00:16:07.258
Priya Raman: Will do.

248
00:16:08.338 --> 00:16:08.888
Diane Okafor: Okay.

249
00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:09.921
Diane Okafor: Thank you.

250
00:16:11.406 --> 00:16:12.357
Diane Okafor: Old business.

251
00:16:12.489 --> 00:16:14.608
Diane Okafor: Item 8a, the pool resurfacing.

252
00:16:14.854 --> 00:16:18.099
Diane Okafor: Priya, where are we on the bids?

253
00:16:19.179 --> 00:16:21.666
Priya Raman: We have two bids so far.

254
00:16:21.740 --> 00:16:27.418
Priya Raman: Aqua Shore Pools came in at $38,400, and Blue Mesa Pool Company at $42,950.

255
00:16:27.523 --> 00:16:32.255
Priya Raman: Both include replastering, a new tile line, and the coping repairs.

256
00:16:32.392 --> 00:16:39.809
Priya Raman: I also asked Ridgeline Pool Services, and they said they could get us a bid by early October.

257
00:16:41.024 --> 00:16:46.501
Grace Lindqvist: And just for reference, the reserve study has $40,000 for resurfacing in 2027,

258
00:16:46.649 --> 00:16:49.355
Grace Lindqvist: so Aqua Shore is under that.

259
00:16:50.705 --> 00:16:55.276
Marcus Bell: Did either of them say how long the job takes?

260
00:16:56.086 --> 00:16:57.305
Priya Raman: About three weeks.

261
00:16:57.602 --> 00:17:01.629
Priya Raman: Both said they'd want to start in March, weather permitting.

262
00:17:02.979 --> 00:17:04.275
Raymond Castillo: What about warranties?

263
00:17:04.504 --> 00:17:07.666
Raymond Castillo: Last time we got burned on the plaster.

264
00:17:08.746 --> 00:17:13.857
Priya Raman: Aqua Shore gives five years on the plaster and Blue Mesa gives seven.

265
00:17:14.148 --> 00:17:16.604
Priya Raman: That's part of the price difference.

266
00:17:17.819 --> 00:17:21.006
Raymond Castillo: Then I'd rather wait for the third bid.

267
00:17:21.118 --> 00:17:27.334
Raymond Castillo: We're not doing the work until spring anyway, and these two are pretty far apart.

268
00:17:28.279 --> 00:17:30.019
Helen's iPhone: I agree with Raymond.

269
00:17:31.099 --> 00:17:31.649
Diane Okafor: Okay.

270
00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:38.033
Diane Okafor: Then I'd entertain a motion to postpone the pool resurfacing decision to the October meeting.

271
00:17:38.843 --> 00:17:39.669
Raymond Castillo: So moved.

272
00:17:40.614 --> 00:17:41.164
Helen's iPhone: Second.

273
00:17:41.704 --> 00:17:43.372
Diane Okafor: Raymond moved, Helen seconded.

274
00:17:43.718 --> 00:17:45.085
Diane Okafor: All in favor?

275
00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:46.310
Raymond Castillo: Aye.

276
00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:46.660
Grace Lindqvist: Aye.

277
00:17:46.795 --> 00:17:47.345
Helen's iPhone: Aye.

278
00:17:47.045 --> 00:17:47.595
Marcus Bell: Aye.

279
00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:48.550
Diane Okafor: Aye.

280
00:17:48.686 --> 00:17:49.236
Diane Okafor: Opposed?

281
00:17:51.936 --> 00:17:54.261
Diane Okafor: Okay, that's five to zero.

282
00:17:54.595 --> 00:17:56.484
Diane Okafor: It's postponed to October.

283
00:17:56.792 --> 00:18:01.257
Diane Okafor: Priya, please get the Ridgeline bid into the October packet.

284
00:18:01.932 --> 00:18:02.710
Priya Raman: Will do.

285
00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:05.190
Diane Okafor: New business.

286
00:18:05.292 --> 00:18:07.794
Diane Okafor: Item 9a, the landscaping contract renewal.

287
00:18:07.882 --> 00:18:10.424
Diane Okafor: Pinecrest's contract runs out October 31st.

288
00:18:10.699 --> 00:18:14.400
Diane Okafor: Priya, can you walk us through the bids?

289
00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:16.030
Priya Raman: Sure.

290
00:18:16.177 --> 00:18:18.702
Priya Raman: Let me share the bid summary.

291
00:18:29.502 --> 00:18:31.803
Priya Raman: Okay, you should see it now.

292
00:18:32.883 --> 00:18:36.427
Priya Raman: So we got three bids for a two-year contract.

293
00:18:36.583 --> 00:18:39.827
Priya Raman: Pinecrest, our current company, bid $5,150 a month.

294
00:18:39.997 --> 00:18:43.820
Priya Raman: Green Way Lawn and Garden bid $4,800 a month,

295
00:18:44.096 --> 00:18:49.785
Priya Raman: but that doesn't include leaf removal or the seasonal flowers, which would be extra.

296
00:18:50.127 --> 00:18:53.706
Priya Raman: And Holloway Landscapes came in at $5,600 a month.

297
00:18:54.786 --> 00:19:00.629
Grace Lindqvist: Wait, I had Holloway at $5,650 in my notes from the bid summary.

298
00:19:02.519 --> 00:19:03.069
Priya Raman: Hmm.

299
00:19:03.369 --> 00:19:08.754
Priya Raman: I don't have it in front of me, so I'd have to double check.

300
00:19:08.920 --> 00:19:10.936
Priya Raman: Either way, they're the highest.

301
00:19:12.286 --> 00:19:14.085
Helen's iPhone: What about the irrigation?

302
00:19:14.355 --> 00:19:17.355
Helen's iPhone: Does Pinecrest's price include the spring startup?

303
00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:18.850
Priya Raman: Yes.

304
00:19:19.118 --> 00:19:23.529
Priya Raman: Pinecrest and Holloway both include the spring startup and the winterizing.

305
00:19:23.798 --> 00:19:26.145
Priya Raman: Green Way charges for those separately.

306
00:19:27.495 --> 00:19:30.555
Helen's iPhone: Do we know anything about Green Way?

307
00:19:30.806 --> 00:19:32.931
Helen's iPhone: I haven't heard of them.

308
00:19:34.011 --> 00:19:38.266
Priya Raman: They maintain two communities near us, Fernhollow Park and Ashbury Ridge.

309
00:19:38.332 --> 00:19:42.167
Priya Raman: I sent both references to the board last week.

310
00:19:43.382 --> 00:19:49.858
Grace Lindqvist: I called the manager at Fernhollow Park, and she said they've been happy with them.

311
00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.633
Grace Lindqvist: But that's one reference.

312
00:19:52.983 --> 00:19:54.981
Raymond Castillo: Honestly, Pinecrest has been good.

313
00:19:55.232 --> 00:19:59.701
Raymond Castillo: They respond quickly, and the entrance has never looked better.

314
00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:02.480
Raymond Castillo: I'd like to stay with them.

315
00:20:03.560 --> 00:20:06.768
Grace Lindqvist: I'm going to push back a little.

316
00:20:07.112 --> 00:20:10.015
Grace Lindqvist: Green Way is $350 a month less.

317
00:20:10.204 --> 00:20:17.313
Grace Lindqvist: That's $8,400 over two years, and we just paid for a pump motor we didn't budget for.

318
00:20:18.528 --> 00:20:26.286
Helen's iPhone: But if you add the leaf removal back in, doesn't Green Way come out about the same?

319
00:20:27.366 --> 00:20:32.020
Priya Raman: Leaf removal was about $3,000 last year, so it narrows the gap,

320
00:20:32.177 --> 00:20:35.970
Priya Raman: but Green Way would still be a little lower.

321
00:20:37.455 --> 00:20:40.583
Marcus Bell: Can I ask about the contract terms?

322
00:20:40.925 --> 00:20:46.199
Marcus Bell: If we sign for two years and they slip, are we stuck?

323
00:20:47.279 --> 00:20:47.829
Priya Raman: No.

324
00:20:47.967 --> 00:20:55.023
Priya Raman: All three contracts have a thirty-day termination clause, so the board can end it with thirty days' notice.

325
00:20:56.373 --> 00:21:00.126
Diane Okafor: For what it's worth, I'd lean toward Pinecrest too.

326
00:21:00.437 --> 00:21:06.869
Diane Okafor: When the irrigation main broke in June, they had a crew out the same day.

327
00:21:07.208 --> 00:21:10.886
Diane Okafor: But I understand Grace's point about the budget.

328
00:21:11.966 --> 00:21:14.055
Grace Lindqvist: I'm not saying they're bad.

329
00:21:14.353 --> 00:21:20.179
Grace Lindqvist: I just think we should be careful this year, with the insurance going up.

330
00:21:21.799 --> 00:21:22.349
Diane Okafor: Okay.

331
00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:25.085
Diane Okafor: I think we've heard the options.

332
00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:27.087
Diane Okafor: Is there a motion?

333
00:21:28.437 --> 00:21:35.828
Raymond Castillo: I move that we renew the contract with Pinecrest Grounds Maintenance for two years at $5,150 per month,

334
00:21:36.162 --> 00:21:37.439
Raymond Castillo: starting November 1st.

335
00:21:38.519 --> 00:21:39.485
Helen's iPhone: I'll second.

336
00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:42.989
Diane Okafor: Moved by Raymond, seconded by Helen.

337
00:21:43.067 --> 00:21:44.444
Diane Okafor: Any more discussion?

338
00:21:48.494 --> 00:21:49.044
Diane Okafor: Okay.

339
00:21:49.265 --> 00:21:53.711
Diane Okafor: Since it's a contract, let's do a roll call vote.

340
00:21:54.005 --> 00:21:54.555
Diane Okafor: Marcus?

341
00:21:55.635 --> 00:21:56.185
Marcus Bell: Okafor?

342
00:21:56.860 --> 00:21:57.410
Diane Okafor: Yes.

343
00:21:58.085 --> 00:21:58.635
Marcus Bell: Castillo?

344
00:21:59.310 --> 00:21:59.860
Raymond Castillo: Yes.

345
00:22:00.535 --> 00:22:01.085
Marcus Bell: Lindquist?

346
00:22:02.165 --> 00:22:02.715
Grace Lindqvist: No.

347
00:22:03.390 --> 00:22:03.940
Marcus Bell: Whitaker?

348
00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:05.840
Helen's iPhone: Yes.

349
00:22:06.515 --> 00:22:07.801
Marcus Bell: And Bell, yes.

350
00:22:08.083 --> 00:22:10.474
Marcus Bell: That's four yes and one no.

351
00:22:11.419 --> 00:22:14.143
Diane Okafor: The motion carries, four to one.

352
00:22:14.455 --> 00:22:19.768
Diane Okafor: Priya, please let Pinecrest know, and send me the contract to sign.

353
00:22:20.578 --> 00:22:26.698
Priya Raman: I'll send it to you by Friday, and I'll let the other two companies know.

354
00:22:28.048 --> 00:22:30.845
Diane Okafor: Item 9b, the reserve study update.

355
00:22:30.964 --> 00:22:31.514
Diane Okafor: Grace?

356
00:22:32.459 --> 00:22:33.009
Grace Lindqvist: Sure.

357
00:22:33.310 --> 00:22:41.416
Grace Lindqvist: Our last full reserve study was done in 2023, and we're supposed to update it every three years.

358
00:22:41.554 --> 00:22:48.910
Grace Lindqvist: Keystone Reserve Advisors sent a proposal for a Level 2 update with a site visit, for $3,200.

359
00:22:48.999 --> 00:22:52.597
Grace Lindqvist: They'd deliver the report in about eight weeks.

360
00:22:52.688 --> 00:22:55.825
Grace Lindqvist: It's in the budget under professional fees.

361
00:22:57.175 --> 00:23:01.213
Marcus Bell: Is that the same firm we used last time?

362
00:23:02.023 --> 00:23:06.538
Grace Lindqvist: Yes, same firm, so they already have our component list.

363
00:23:07.753 --> 00:23:10.126
Raymond Castillo: Will they look at the roads?

364
00:23:10.372 --> 00:23:14.353
Raymond Castillo: The asphalt on Larkspur Lane is getting pretty bad.

365
00:23:15.298 --> 00:23:18.716
Grace Lindqvist: Yes, the roads are one of the components.

366
00:23:19.931 --> 00:23:24.567
Diane Okafor: Will we have the report before we adopt the 2027 budget?

367
00:23:25.647 --> 00:23:26.567
Grace Lindqvist: Probably not.

368
00:23:26.833 --> 00:23:30.363
Grace Lindqvist: The budget has to be adopted in November,

369
00:23:30.634 --> 00:23:38.617
Grace Lindqvist: so we'll use the 2023 study for the 2027 reserve contribution and adjust next year if we need to.

370
00:23:40.507 --> 00:23:51.295
Grace Lindqvist: So I'll move that we approve the proposal from Keystone Reserve Advisors for a Level 2 reserve study update at a cost of $3,200.

371
00:23:52.105 --> 00:23:52.655
Marcus Bell: Second.

372
00:23:53.465 --> 00:23:54.857
Diane Okafor: Moved and seconded.

373
00:23:55.161 --> 00:23:56.495
Diane Okafor: All in favor?

374
00:23:57.035 --> 00:23:57.585
Raymond Castillo: Aye.

375
00:23:57.485 --> 00:23:58.035
Helen's iPhone: Aye.

376
00:23:57.835 --> 00:23:58.385
Grace Lindqvist: Aye.

377
00:23:58.385 --> 00:23:58.935
Marcus Bell: Aye.

378
00:23:59.340 --> 00:23:59.890
Diane Okafor: Aye.

379
00:23:59.991 --> 00:24:00.541
Diane Okafor: Opposed?

380
00:24:00.651 --> 00:24:01.201
Diane Okafor: Abstaining?

381
00:24:03.901 --> 00:24:06.734
Diane Okafor: Okay, that passes five to zero.

382
00:24:07.679 --> 00:24:15.380
Grace Lindqvist: I'll sign the engagement letter and get it back to them by the end of the month.

383
00:24:16.730 --> 00:24:21.871
Diane Okafor: Item 9c, the architectural request for a fence at 18 Thistle Court.

384
00:24:22.082 --> 00:24:24.736
Diane Okafor: Helen, that came through your committee.

385
00:24:26.086 --> 00:24:26.636
Helen's iPhone: Yes.

386
00:24:26.727 --> 00:24:34.845
Helen's iPhone: The owners at 18 Thistle Court asked to put in a six-foot cedar privacy fence around their back yard.

387
00:24:34.971 --> 00:24:39.137
Helen's iPhone: Our guidelines cap rear yard fences at five feet.

388
00:24:39.372 --> 00:24:41.696
Helen's iPhone: The committee met last week,

389
00:24:41.806 --> 00:24:46.958
Helen's iPhone: and we recommend approving it at a maximum height of five feet,

390
00:24:47.139 --> 00:24:49.398
Helen's iPhone: in the approved cedar style.

391
00:24:49.610 --> 00:24:53.513
Helen's iPhone: So that's the committee's recommendation as a motion.

392
00:24:54.863 --> 00:24:58.210
Raymond Castillo: Did they say why they want six feet?

393
00:24:59.290 --> 00:25:04.340
Helen's iPhone: They have a large dog that can jump a five-foot fence.

394
00:25:04.685 --> 00:25:12.351
Helen's iPhone: The committee talked about it, but the guidelines are clear, and we didn't want to set a precedent.

395
00:25:12.475 --> 00:25:18.890
Helen's iPhone: They can still apply for a variance if they want to go through that process.

396
00:25:19.118 --> 00:25:23.999
Helen's iPhone: We also got letters from both neighbors, and neither one objected.

397
00:25:25.079 --> 00:25:29.669
Diane Okafor: Since that comes from the committee, it doesn't need a second.

398
00:25:29.840 --> 00:25:30.773
Diane Okafor: Any discussion?

399
00:25:32.393 --> 00:25:39.204
Marcus Bell: Just so everyone knows, they're my next-door neighbors, so I'm going to abstain on this one.

400
00:25:40.149 --> 00:25:40.699
Diane Okafor: Understood.

401
00:25:40.923 --> 00:25:48.801
Diane Okafor: All in favor of approving the fence at a maximum of five feet, in the approved cedar style?

402
00:25:49.476 --> 00:25:50.026
Raymond Castillo: Aye.

403
00:25:49.826 --> 00:25:50.376
Grace Lindqvist: Aye.

404
00:25:50.646 --> 00:25:51.196
Helen's iPhone: Aye.

405
00:25:51.736 --> 00:25:52.286
Diane Okafor: Aye.

406
00:25:52.403 --> 00:25:52.953
Diane Okafor: Opposed?

407
00:25:55.653 --> 00:25:57.345
Diane Okafor: And Marcus is abstaining.

408
00:25:57.677 --> 00:26:02.156
Diane Okafor: So that's four in favor, none opposed, and one abstention.

409
00:26:02.231 --> 00:26:03.627
Diane Okafor: The motion carries.

410
00:26:04.707 --> 00:26:08.976
Priya Raman: I'll get the approval letter out to the owners by Friday.

411
00:26:10.596 --> 00:26:11.146
Diane Okafor: Okay.

412
00:26:11.266 --> 00:26:13.760
Diane Okafor: That brings us to executive session.

413
00:26:13.957 --> 00:26:19.189
Diane Okafor: The board needs to discuss a delinquent account and a contract matter.

414
00:26:19.455 --> 00:26:26.842
Diane Okafor: Homeowners, Priya will move you to the waiting room, and we'll bring you back when we're done.

415
00:26:27.084 --> 00:26:29.590
Diane Okafor: It should be about ten minutes.

416
00:26:29.830 --> 00:26:31.742
Diane Okafor: The time is 7:26.

417
00:26:32.822 --> 00:26:34.388
Priya Raman: Okay, moving everyone now.

418
00:26:43.838 --> 00:26:46.914
Priya Raman: Okay, so the first one is account 1147.

419
00:26:47.057 --> 00:26:54.912
Priya Raman: They're now at $4,100 and change, and they didn't respond to the second letter or the certified letter.

420
00:26:55.722 --> 00:26:58.958
Marcus Bell: Wait, sorry, Diane, is the recording still going?

421
00:27:00.038 --> 00:27:00.588
Diane Okafor: Oh.

422
00:27:00.696 --> 00:27:01.631
Diane Okafor: Good catch.

423
00:27:01.727 --> 00:27:03.098
Diane Okafor: Stopping it now.

424
00:27:05.123 --> 00:27:07.793
Diane Okafor: Okay, the recording is back on.

425
00:27:08.005 --> 00:27:10.110
Diane Okafor: We're back in open session.

426
00:27:10.364 --> 00:27:11.243
Diane Okafor: It's 7:35.

427
00:27:11.341 --> 00:27:13.510
Diane Okafor: Priya, is everyone back in?

428
00:27:14.860 --> 00:27:16.090
Priya Raman: Yes, everyone's back.

429
00:27:17.170 --> 00:27:18.102
Diane Okafor: Thank you.

430
00:27:18.281 --> 00:27:24.188
Diane Okafor: In executive session, the board discussed one delinquent account and a vendor contract matter,

431
00:27:24.497 --> 00:27:28.293
Diane Okafor: and no action was taken in executive session.

432
00:27:28.400 --> 00:27:32.018
Diane Okafor: Is there a motion on the delinquent account?

433
00:27:33.368 --> 00:27:39.193
Grace Lindqvist: I move that we refer account number 1147 to the association's attorney for collection.

434
00:27:40.003 --> 00:27:40.553
Raymond Castillo: Second.

435
00:27:41.228 --> 00:27:42.495
Diane Okafor: All in favor?

436
00:27:43.035 --> 00:27:43.585
Raymond Castillo: Aye.

437
00:27:43.385 --> 00:27:43.935
Grace Lindqvist: Aye.

438
00:27:44.070 --> 00:27:44.620
Helen's iPhone: Aye.

439
00:27:44.420 --> 00:27:44.970
Marcus Bell: Aye.

440
00:27:45.375 --> 00:27:45.925
Diane Okafor: Aye.

441
00:27:46.057 --> 00:27:46.607
Diane Okafor: Opposed?

442
00:27:49.307 --> 00:27:52.147
Diane Okafor: Okay, that's unanimous, five to zero.

